  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q7",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Find the gradient of the tangent at each point given on the inverse function of:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=(3x+1)(x-4)^5$ at $(-10,3)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac1{47}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=3(x-4)^5+5(3x+1)(x-4)^4\\\\&=(x-4)^4(18x-7)\\\\(f^{-1})'(-10)&=\\frac{1}{f'(3)}\\\\&=\\frac{1}{(3-4)^4(54-7)}\\\\&=\\frac1{47}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=(x-3)\\cos x$ at $(-3,0)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$",
          "worked": "Writing $f(x)=(x-3)\\cos x$,\n$$\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\cos x-(x-3)\\sin x\\\\f'(0)&=1\\\\(f^{-1})'(-3)&=\\frac{1}{f'(0)}\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{x^3}{3x-4}$ at $(4,2)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Undefined; the inverse curve has a vertical tangent.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{3x^2(3x-4)-3x^3}{(3x-4)^2}\\\\&=\\frac{6x^2(x-2)}{(3x-4)^2}\\\\f'(2)&=0\\end{aligned}$$\nThe corresponding tangent to the original curve is horizontal. Its reflection is vertical, so the gradient of the inverse curve at $(4,2)$ is undefined.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$y=x\\ln x$ at $(0,1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$",
          "worked": "Writing $f(x)=x\\ln x$,\n$$\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\ln x+1\\\\(f^{-1})'(0)&=\\frac{1}{f'(1)}\\\\&=\\frac{1}{\\ln1+1}\\\\&=1\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$y=\\dfrac{\\sin(3x)}{x^2}$ at $\\left(-\\dfrac4{\\pi^2},\\dfrac\\pi2\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{\\pi^3}{16}$",
          "worked": "Writing $f(x)=\\dfrac{\\sin(3x)}{x^2}$,\n$$\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{3x^2\\cos(3x)-2x\\sin(3x)}{x^4}\\\\&=\\frac{3x\\cos(3x)-2\\sin(3x)}{x^3}\\\\f'\\left(\\frac\\pi2\\right)&=\\frac{3\\frac\\pi2\\cos\\frac{3\\pi}2-2\\sin\\frac{3\\pi}2}{(\\frac\\pi2)^3}\\\\&=\\frac{16}{\\pi^3}\\\\(f^{-1})'\\left(-\\frac4{\\pi^2}\\right)&=\\frac{1}{f'(\\frac\\pi2)}\\\\&=\\frac{\\pi^3}{16}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      }
    ]
  },
